Write standard CSS rules implementing this design specification. Each outer key is a selector; each inner key is a valid CSS property and its value is the desired styling. One rule per selector, colon between property/value, semicolon after EVERY declaration. No JSON, JavaScript, explanations or extra rules in the output. Design specification:
{
  "*": {
    "box-sizing": "border-box"
  },
  "html, body": {
    "margin": "0",
    "width": "100%"
  },
  "body": {
    "font": "13px system-ui, sans-serif",
    "background": "#0e1013",
    "color": "#edf0f4"
  },
  "button, input": {
    "font": "inherit"
  }
}

